.TH ARVIO-TASK 5 "2026-10-26" "arvio 0.2.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
arvio-task \- the task folder that arvio reads and writes (format version 1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
my\-task/
    task.toml      the task card
    items.jsonl    one item per line
    labels.jsonl   written by arvio
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A task is one folder with three files.
Your project writes
.I task.toml
and
.IR items.jsonl .
.BR arvio (1)
writes
.IR labels.jsonl .
Your project never imports arvio: it writes the first two files and reads the third.
.PP
.B arvio check
validates all three and exits 1 on any problem.
A problem in a JSONL file names the file and the line.
A problem in
.I task.toml
names the file and the setting, for example
.BR "choice 3 hotkey" .
Unknown keys are errors, so a typo never silently drops a setting.
.SH task.toml
The task card is a TOML file.
It holds the question, the choices and what each one means, follow-up questions, and how to compare the labels with the judge.
.SS Top-level keys
.TP
.B format
Required. The format version. It is
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B title
Required. The name shown in the inbox.
.TP
.B purpose
What the labels are for.
.TP
.B question
Required. The question the labeler answers for each item.
.TP
.B rules
A list of short rules shown with the question.
.TP
.B session_size
Items per session, from 1 to 100. The default is 10.
.TP
.B seconds_per_item
A first time estimate per item, from 1 to 3600, used until arvio has measured the labeler's pace.
The default is 60.
.TP
.B pin
A string that changes when the judge's instructions change.
It is part of the task version.
.SS [[choices]]
One table per answer.
Every task needs a choice with the key
.B cant_tell
and at least one other choice.
.TP
.B key
1 to 40 characters from
.BR "a\-z 0\-9 _" .
.TP
.B hotkey
One lowercase letter or digit.
Hotkeys are unique across the whole card, in the choices and in every follow-up option.
.B n
is reserved for the note field.
.TP
.B label
The text shown on the button.
.TP
.B meaning
What the answer means.
.TP
.B example
An optional example.
.SS [[followups]]
Optional follow-up questions, asked after a choice is picked.
.TP
.B key
Same rules as a choice's key.
.TP
.B when
Required. The list of choice keys that show this follow-up.
.TP
.B kind
One of
.BR single ,
.BR multi ,
.B text
or
.BR edit .
.TP
.B required
True or false. The default is false.
.TP
.B prompt
The question shown.
.TP
.B options
For
.B single
and
.BR multi :
a list of tables with
.BR key ,
.BR hotkey ,
.B label
and
.BR meaning .
.TP
.B fields
For
.BR edit :
a list of tables with
.BR key ,
.B label
and
.BR multiline .
Each field starts with the item's
.BI prefill[ key ]
value.
A required
.B edit
follow-up needs at least one field changed from its prefill, or the page does not save it.
.SS [agreement]
Optional. How to compare the labels with the judge.
.TP
.B judge_field
The key in each item's
.B judge
object.
.TP
.B map
A table from each judge value to the list of choices that agree with it.
A choice may appear in at most one list.
.B cant_tell
may not appear.
A choice in no list counts as disagreeing with every judge value.
A judge value that is not a string, such as
.BR true ,
is written in its JSON text:
.B "map = { true = [\(dqcorrect\(dq], false = [\(dqwrong\(dq] }"
.TP
.B compare
Optional. A list of tables with
.B followup
(a
.B single
or
.B text
follow-up) and
.B judge_field
(the judge field to compare it with).
.SS [gate]
Optional. A pass rule for
.BR "arvio report" .
It needs an
.B [agreement]
section.
.TP
.B min_n
At least this many items compared with the judge. 1 or more.
.TP
.B kappa_lower
The low end of kappa's 95% range must be at least this. Between \-1 and 1.
.TP
.B agreement_lower
The low end of the raw agreement's 95% range must be at least this. Between 0 and 1.
.PP
A gate sets
.BR kappa_lower ,
.B agreement_lower
or both.
It passes only when every one it sets holds, with at least
.B min_n
items compared.
.SS Task version
arvio hashes the question, each choice's key and meaning, each follow-up (key,
.BR when ,
kind,
.BR required ,
prompt, option keys and meanings, field keys) and
.B pin
into a 12-character task version.
Every label records the version it was made under.
If you change any of these, older labels stop counting, and their items come back as unlabeled.
.B "arvio status"
shows how many older labels there are.
.PP
The title, purpose, rules, labels, hotkeys, examples,
.BR session_size ,
.B seconds_per_item
and the order of choices, follow-ups and options are not part of the hash.
Changing them keeps your labels.
.SH items.jsonl
One JSON object per line.
.TP
.B id
Required. Unique. Up to 200 characters from
.BR "A\-Z a\-z 0\-9 . _ : \-" ,
starting with a letter or digit.
Use a hash of the item's content, so that exporting again keeps the same ids.
The page does not show the id while the labeler works, but the data the page loads contains it.
Keep values from
.B meta
and
.B judge
(a model name, a run number) out of it.
.B "arvio check"
warns when an id contains one.
.TP
.B display
Required. The blocks shown to the labeler, in order. At least one.
.TP
.B prefill
Strings that start the
.B edit
fields, keyed by field key.
A key that is no edit field on the card is an error.
.TP
.B judge
The judge's answer.
arvio never sends it to the page until the session ends.
.B null
or a missing key means no judge for this item.
When the card has
.BR [agreement] ,
the object must hold
.B judge_field
with a value from
.BR map .
.TP
.B meta
Anything you want for report buckets (see
.BR "arvio report \-\-by" ).
It is never sent to the page.
.SS Display blocks
.TP
.B text
Keys:
.BR text ;
optional
.BR title ,
.B mono
(true or false),
.B highlight
(a list of exact substrings of
.BR text ,
spaces and line breaks included) and
.B collapsed
(true or false).
.TP
.B diff
Keys:
.B text
(a unified diff); optional
.B title
and
.BR collapsed .
.TP
.B fields
Keys:
.B fields
(a list of
.B [label, value]
string pairs); optional
.B title
and
.BR collapsed .
.PP
All text is shown as plain text.
Nothing is rendered as HTML or Markdown.
.PP
In both JSONL files, a key that appears twice in one object, \fBNaN\fR, \fBInfinity\fR, and half of a surrogate pair are errors.
.PP
Write
.I items.jsonl
to a temporary file and rename it into place, so that arvio never reads half a file.
Keep every item that already has a label under the current card: a label whose item is gone is an error.
A label under an older card whose item is gone only gets a warning.
.SH labels.jsonl
arvio appends one line per event and syncs it to disk before answering the page.
There are two kinds of line.
.PP
A
.B label
row:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"kind": "label", "item_id": "q01\-5d1c2e", "item_hash": "9b04e1c2a7f3",
 "task_version": "c41d09a2b6e1", "answer": "wrong",
 "followups": {"why": "unsupported"}, "note": "", "seconds": 38.4,
 "labeled_at": "2026\-10\-19T16:02:11Z", "labeler": "sam",
 "session": "s\-20261019T160000Z\-ab12"}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A
.B reveal
row:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"kind": "reveal", "item_ids": ["q01\-5d1c2e"],
 "task_version": "c41d09a2b6e1", "at": "2026\-10\-19T16:09:40Z",
 "session": "s\-20261019T160000Z\-ab12"}
.fi
.RE
.IP \(bu 2
.B followups
holds one value per answered follow-up: an option key (\fBsingle\fR), a list of option keys (\fBmulti\fR), a string (\fBtext\fR), or an object of field values (\fBedit\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
.B item_hash
is a hash of what the labeler saw (\fBdisplay\fR and \fBprefill\fR).
If it no longer matches the item, the item changed after it was labeled, and
.B "arvio check"
warns.
.IP \(bu 2
.B seconds
counts only the time the page was visible, from 0 to 86400.
.IP \(bu 2
.B labeler
is the value of
.BR ARVIO_LABELER ,
or the login name if it is not set.
.SS Reading the log
Go through the lines in order and keep only rows whose
.B task_version
matches the current card.
For each item, the latest
.B label
row wins.
A
.B reveal
row locks those of the items it names that have a label by then, because the labeler saw the judge's answer.
arvio refuses any later label for them under the same version.
An item that a reveal names before it has a label stays open.
.PP
You do not have to write this reader yourself.
.B "arvio labels"
applies the rule and prints one JSON line per labeled item.
.PP
A last line with no newline that does not parse is a write that was cut short, or one still in progress.
Readers skip it with a warning.
Before its next append, arvio moves that text to
.I labels.jsonl.torn
and starts on a clean line.
.PP
.B "arvio check"
also warns, without failing, when a label comes after its item's reveal (it is ignored), when a reveal names an item with no label, when an item changed after it was labeled, and when an item's id contains one of its
.B meta
or
.B judge
values.
.SH THE INBOX
.B "arvio add"
checks a task folder and records its absolute path in
.IR $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/tasks.json ,
which is
.I ~/.arvio/tasks.json
by default.
.B "arvio remove"
takes it off.
The task's files stay.
The inbox holds paths only, never items or labels.
.PP
.B "arvio add \-\-import"
first copies
.I task.toml
and
.I items.jsonl
into
.IR $ARVIO_DATA_DIR/tasks/NAME ,
and adds that copy.
Labels are written there.
The project's
.I labels.jsonl
is never copied.
Running the import again replaces the card and the items and keeps the labels.
It is refused, and nothing changes, if the labels would then name an item that is gone, or if a page has the folder open.
.PP
An inbox entry can carry
.BR """archived"": true" .
.B "arvio archive"
sets it and
.B "arvio unarchive"
removes it.
The folder itself never moves.
An archived task is hidden from the page's Active tab and from
.BR "arvio status" ,
and it appears on the Archived tab and under
.BR "arvio status \-\-archived" .
The page cannot start a session on an archived task until it is moved back.
.SH EXAMPLES
A small card with two choices and the required
.BR cant_tell :
.PP
.RS
.nf
format = 1
title = "Is the draft answer right?"
question = "Does the draft answer match the source text?"

[[choices]]
key = "correct"
hotkey = "c"
label = "Correct"
meaning = "The answer says what the source says."

[[choices]]
key = "wrong"
hotkey = "w"
label = "Wrong"
meaning = "The answer contradicts the source."

[[choices]]
key = "cant_tell"
hotkey = "u"
label = "Can't tell"
meaning = "The text shown is not enough to decide."

[agreement]
judge_field = "verdict"
map = { pass = ["correct"], fail = ["wrong"] }
.fi
.RE
.PP
One line of
.IR items.jsonl :
.PP
.RS
.nf
{"id": "q01\-5d1c2e", "display": [{"kind": "text", "title": "Question",
 "text": "When does the library open?"}, {"kind": "text",
 "title": "Draft answer", "text": "09:00"}],
 "judge": {"verdict": "pass"}, "meta": {"topic": "opening\-hours"}}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A complete made-up task is in
.I examples/hello
in the arvio repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arvio (1)
.PP
The same format is written out in
.I docs/format.md
in the arvio repository, https://github.com/jboho/arvio.
